\DOC DISCARD_FLAGS_TAC

\TYPE {DISCARD_FLAGS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Deletes from the assumption list every hypothesis stating the value of a
processor condition flag in a state, leaving the conclusion untouched.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. The tactic scans the assumptions and drops those of the
form asserting that reading a status flag component of a machine state is
equivalent to some boolean expression. All other assumptions — register and
memory reads, arithmetic side conditions, loaded-code and frame assumptions —
are kept in their original order.
{
       A, f1 ... fn ?- t
     ===================== DISCARD_FLAGS_TAC
             A ?- t
}
\noindent Here {f1 ... fn} are the flag-valued assumptions removed; n may be
zero.

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show this single kind of outcome, always on goals that do
contain such flag assumptions.

\ENDDOC
